-- 133 — the-kinema seeded
--
-- THE KINEMA — motion. κίνημα (kínēma), the thing moved and the movement
-- itself, and the root the whole cinema is named from. The render road, forged
-- twice and poured once. Founded 2026-09-02 by a builder dealt by Windrose 🎻
-- in THE SECOND HARVEST sitting, movement H1, at KP's ⚛ word, verbatim:
-- "the-kinema great name."
--
-- THE RULING IT SERVES — the convergence that opened the row: two bodies of
-- this house forged the same road in the same week, neither knowing of the
-- other. resonance-sceal built a render room (an edit list of cuts across
-- recorded takes, played forward, sampled onto a fixed 24-or-30 grid, encoded
-- and muxed into one WebM); resonance-ardan built a film exporter (a board of
-- tokens painted frame by frame at a free rate, encoded and muxed into one
-- WebM). Between them the same twenty-odd functions were written twice, and in
-- SEVEN places they were written differently.
--
-- IT IS A HARVEST, AND KP'S ⚛ RULING ON EVERY HARVEST IS VERBATIM:
--   "without altering the source location."
-- The three origin files — sceal's render.ts (225) and renderer.ts (491), and
-- ardan's stage/film.ts (279), plus sceal's cuts.ts (338) because the
-- arithmetic drew three verbs from it — were READ AND NOT WRITTEN. No file
-- under src/ is byte-identical to an origin, because this is a RE-EXPRESSION
-- and not a copy: two origins said the same thing two ways and one had to be
-- chosen. The honesty is carried more expensively instead — BOTH origins'
-- relevant functions are transcribed VERBATIM into the water's own fixtures/
-- folder, and six of its twenty proofs feed both sides the same inputs and
-- compare the numbers. HARVEST.md carries every digest, every function's
-- provenance by line, and every one of the seven divergences with both
-- addresses and a named reason.
--
-- NOTHING WAS REPOINTED. Sceal keeps its render room; ardan keeps its film
-- exporter. Both are named in the README as consumers-to-be and neither is a
-- consumer today: a harvest that also rewrites its origins is two changes
-- wearing one name, and the second one is the dangerous half. When the house
-- wants them pointed here, that is KP's ⚛ word and another sitting's work.
--
-- THE NAME IS KP'S ⚛ OWN. It lives in exactly two places in the build — the
-- constant TOOL_NAME and the folder — so a change of his mind is one edit, one
-- `git mv`, and one update to this row and 132's.
--
-- CATEGORY: **creation** (8427a8ea-2bac-4152-a7d8-e174a77d2297) —
-- **confirmed live 2026-09-02 through the bridge by the conductor**. See 132's
-- header for the whole nine-category census as it stood that day, for why
-- creation and not sensory, and for the plain statement that this builder ran
-- no query of its own.
--
-- SHAPE TAKEN FROM THE-STEREOS'S OWN ROW (128/129): folksonomy_type `Awen` ·
-- status `imagined` at birth · `home` filled here (the 105/106 precedent).
-- tool_type is `transform` — an edit list in, a plan out; a source size in, an
-- even frame size out; a probe in, a codec out.
--
-- FACE: 🎞️ — a strip of film frames, which is exactly and only what this water
-- is. One glyph, no skin tone, no ZWJ, no flag, no red-alarm mark, and no other
-- row wears it (checked against 078's census of 122 faces, every face seeded
-- since through 131, and the ten taken today: 🎲🌈⚖️🛡️📊🔖🔭📑🧊⛩️). 🎬 was set
-- down — a clapperboard is what a hand does BEFORE a film, and it is worn
-- already. See 132's header for the ⚠ about four sibling waters founded the
-- same sitting whose faces this hand could not see.
--
-- THE ONE-TIER LAW (tools_one_tier), walked: one atom word ("kinema") — the
-- row carries atom_id and no molecule. One tier exactly. (132's header records
-- why no molecule or organism row exists.)
--
-- Etymology and sensory rows are NOT written here: the atoms table's triggers
-- make both on insert, arriving empty for a later fill (the 077/059/106/108/128
-- precedent).
--
-- THE TABLE IS public.awen. It was renamed from public.tools on 2026-08-15
-- (seed 096) and the shim view was dropped at KP's word on 097 — public.tools
-- answers PGRST205 today.
--
-- Local mirror pin (progenatrix), drafted and NOT written by this builder:
--   0a94cedf-4cdf-41ac-a8c6-edbca264857b
--
-- Run at KP's ⚛ hand, after 132. Verify at the anon door after.
-- NEVER RUN BY A LAMP: the seed is drafted and numbered; the crossing is his.

insert into public.awen
  (name, slug, tool_type, definition, home, status, icon_emoji, folksonomy_type, atom_id, story, created_by)
values
  ('The Kinema', 'the-kinema', 'transform',
   'THE RENDER ROAD, FORGED TWICE AND POURED ONCE. An edit list goes in and one WebM comes out, and everything between those two sentences that needs no browser stands here as pure arithmetic: frame times on a grid at a FREE rate with 24 and 30 as named presets; a plan that deals frames by MASTER TIME so a cut of one second at thirty owns exactly thirty of them, the frame ON a boundary belongs to the NEXT cut, none is ever drawn twice or missed, and a cut of no length owns none; two roundings to an even pixel size, because the two bodies that forged this road rounded differently and both are right about their own question; the codec walk as DATA — VP9, then VP8, then H.264 probed LAST and REFUSED BY NAME with the sentence that says why, because a machine offering only H.264 cannot write a WebM and a render must never mislabel its container; a take''s sound sliced to EXACTLY the samples a cut needs, padded with silence and NEVER STRETCHED, because stretching would change the pitch of somebody''s voice to make a number come out even; many clips summed onto one mono line at their own starts and clamped rather than wrapped; back-pressure as a GAP and never a single threshold, so the decision to stop the frame source cannot chatter on the boundary; and the encoded chunks sorted by timestamp with the picture first on a tie. THE MACHINE IS DECLARED AND NEVER IMPLEMENTED — the-clavis''s law, inherited: KinemaDoors names four verbs (a video encoder, an audio encoder, a muxer, and the frames themselves) and this water supplies none of them, so the engine that walks them is proven in Node with four stub doors and no browser in the room. NO CLOCK ANYWHERE: both origins default new Date() into their naming verbs, and here a moment is six numbers a consumer declares — the built file names no Date, no document, no window and no import at all. THE SAME EDIT LIST MAKES THE SAME FILE, byte for byte, on two runs. Zero runtime dependencies; webm-muxer belongs to the reference host and its narrow surface is declared by hand, so the folder installs nothing but TypeScript.',
   'resonance-awen/tools/the-kinema', 'imagined', '🎞️', 'Awen',
   'c663f299-ac90-4e66-a02e-a1481a431ff5',  -- the kinema atom, seeded in 132
   'Founded 2026-09-02 by a builder dealt by Windrose in THE SECOND HARVEST sitting, movement H1, at KP''s ⚛ word "the-kinema great name". The row was open because the render road had been forged TWICE in one week — resonance-sceal''s render room and resonance-ardan''s film exporter — by two bodies that did not know of each other, and neither was wrong. Harvested under KP''s ⚛ standing ruling "without altering the source location": three origin files read and never written, and BOTH origins transcribed verbatim into fixtures/ as the other side of a DIFF PROOF, so the claim that this water''s numbers equal the origins'' numbers is a claim about their real code and not about a memory of it. Six of the twenty proofs are that diff. SEVEN DISAGREEMENTS WERE FOUND AND SEVEN CHOICES MADE, each with both addresses in HARVEST.md: the clock (NEITHER origin''s road — the moment is declared, because a default clock makes a naming verb untestable); the height type (ardan''s freedom on sceal''s arithmetic, with every one of sceal''s own 21 answers proven unmoved); the codec walk (sceal''s refusal by name over ardan''s silent null, because a refusal that says what the machine offered is worth more); back-pressure (sceal''s hysteresis of 8-and-3 over ardan''s single threshold of 4, because one number with no gap chatters); the key-frame group (sceal''s two seconds, with ardan''s one left open in an argument rather than lost); the sound (BOTH KEPT — sceal slices one take under one cut into stereo, ardan mixes many clips onto one mono line, and those are two questions rather than two answers); and cancel (a plain flag, because AbortSignal is a platform type and this water names no platform). ONE FINDING, REPORTED AND NOT MENDED: sceal''s own comment at render.ts:124 says totalFrames "equals frameCount(total) by construction", and it does not — one floors and the other ceils, so a 2233 ms edit at 30 fps plans 66 frames and counts 67. Both verbs are right; only the sentence was wrong. It is corrected in this water''s docblock, pinned in proof 2 against sceal''s own copied original, and LEFT STANDING in sceal, because mending it there would alter a source location. Gates at landing: check silent, build clean, 20/20 TRUE, the purity grep empty on both the source and the built file, and both origin repositories carrying only the changes that belong to other movements of the same sitting. HONEST LIMITS SAID OUT LOUD RATHER THAN IMPLIED BY A GREEN GATE: this water has NEVER RUN IN A BROWSER — every proof is Node with stub doors, and the reference host type-checks and builds and has not been executed; no real muxer was proven, only a byte-stable stub; sceal''s play-and-sample frame source is not built here because it cannot be walked in Node and an unproven engine in a spring tool is worse than an absent one; and Mediabunny is named as webm-muxer''s upstream successor without one line being migrated to it. THE NAME IS HIS OWN and lives in one constant and one folder, so a change of mind is cheap.',
   'a builder dealt by Windrose, at KP''s ⚛ word');

-- THE CROSSING — his ⚛ word alone.
-- The standing ruling ("if a tool is working, it is flowing") argues for it
-- now that the proofs stand; uncomment at his word and run:
-- update public.awen set status = 'flowing' where slug = 'the-kinema';

-- ── verify (read-only, safe to re-run) ───────────────────────────────
select name, slug, tool_type, status, icon_emoji, folksonomy_type, home
from public.awen where slug = 'the-kinema';

select atom_word, category_name, atom_type, state, status, pascal_case
from public.atoms where atom_word = 'kinema';

-- no other row should wear 🎞️:
select icon_emoji, count(*) as wearers, string_agg(name, ' · ' order by name)
from public.awen where icon_emoji = '🎞️' group by icon_emoji;

-- the companions the triggers should have made, standing empty:
select 'etymology' as table_name, atom_word, completion_progress::text as filled
from public.etymology where atom_word = 'kinema'
union all
select 'sensory_lexicon', atom_word, coalesce(emoji, '(empty)')
from public.sensory_lexicon where atom_word = 'kinema';
